DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkllddllooaadd() system call loads a kld file into the kernel using the ker‐
     nel linker.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The kkllddllooaadd() system call returns the fileid of the kld file which was
     loaded into the kernel.  If an error occurs, kkllddllooaadd() will return -1 and
     set _e_r_r_n_o to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The named file is loaded unless:

     [EPERM]            You do not have access to read the file or link it
                        with the kernel.  You should be the root user to be
                        able to use the kklldd system calls.

     [EFAULT]           Bad address encountered when adding kld info into the
                        kernel space.

     [ENOMEM]           There is no memory to load the file into the kernel.

     [ENOENT]           The file was not found.

     [ENOEXEC]          The file format of _f_i_l_e was unrecognized.

     [EEXIST]           The supplied _f_i_l_e has already been loaded.

